    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nThis plugin is really cool. I was amazed that when my tmux window is resized, there's an animation for it.\r\n\r\nBut for some reason, when I drag my tmux window to become larger, the animation plays and then my cmdheight option becomes 1 (I default to 0)\r\n\r\nI'm not sure where it went wrong. I'm using AtroNvim community setting: https://github.com/AstroNvim/astrocommunity/tree/main/lua/astrocommunity/scrolling/mini-animate\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open nvim\r\n2. open neo-tree\r\n3. enlarge nvim window\r\n4. let animation happen\r\n5. cmdheight is now 1\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ncmdheight stays 0\n\n### Actual behavior\n\ncmdheight becomes 1",
