        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, the solution for this problem was conflicting with a more Neovim centered problem described in #2368 (resizing Neovim window when it is done by adjusting 'cmdheight'). At the moment I don't see a concise and robust solution that could satisfy both use cases, so this one has to be accepted as a known limitation. Or my honest suggestion would be to not use animations that have side effects (i.e. \"scroll\" and \"resize\"), as they are quite problematic.",
